+      <div id="scriptPreview" class="preview" aria-live="polite"><p class="muted">Choose a saved script or create one.</p></div>
+      <div class="editor-actions"><div class="actions"><button id="saveScript" class="primary" disabled>Save disabled</button><button id="discardDraft" disabled>Discard draft</button></div><div class="actions"><button id="exportScript" disabled>Export</button><button id="deleteScript" class="danger" disabled>Delete</button></div></div>
+      <div class="activation"><label class="toggle"><input id="scriptEnabled" type="checkbox" disabled> Enable this saved script</label><p id="activationHelp" class="muted">Enable the userscript module to run enabled scripts on future page loads. Reload open pages after changing a script.</p></div>
+    </section>
+  </section>
+  <details class="card compatibility"><summary>Supported userscript features</summary><p>Metadata: @name, @namespace, @version, @description, @match, @exclude-match, @run-at and @noframes. Scripts use separate isolated worlds by default. @inject-into page is available only with @grant none.</p><p>APIs: GM.info / GM_info, GM.addStyle / GM_addStyle, and asynchronous GM.getValue, GM.setValue, GM.deleteValue and GM.listValues. Values are local and private to each script.</p><p>This is a focused userscript manager, not full Violentmonkey compatibility. Legacy synchronous storage, privileged network requests, @include, @require and @resource are unsupported. The editor reports unsupported features before saving. Disabling prevents future runs; it cannot undo JavaScript that already ran.</p><p>Only enable scripts whose code and site access you trust. Scripts can read and change the pages they match. BlockAds does not fetch scripts; a script you enable can itself make web requests.</p></details>
+</main>
+<dialog id="confirmDialog"><form method="dialog"><h2 id="confirmTitle">Discard changes?</h2><p id="confirmText"></p><div class="actions"><button value="cancel" autofocus>Cancel</button><button id="confirmAccept" value="accept" class="danger">Continue</button></div></form></dialog>
+<script src="userscripts-core.js"></script><script src="manager.js"></script>
+</body>
+</html>
